.TH TUI_VIEWDOC_OPEN 3 2026-11-21 "libtuikit 2.0" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_viewdoc_open, tui_viewdoc_handle, tui_viewdoc_render, tui_viewdoc_free, tui_viewdoc_text,
tui_viewdoc_check \- the help page and the view description
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/viewdoc.h>
.PP
.BI "int  tui_viewdoc_open(tui_viewdoc_page *" p ", const tui_viewdoc *" view ,
.BI "                      const char *const *" common ", int " ncommon );
.BI "tui_dialog_state tui_viewdoc_handle(tui_viewdoc_page *" p ", const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "void tui_viewdoc_render(tui_viewdoc_page *" p ", tui_canvas " c );
.BI "void tui_viewdoc_free(tui_viewdoc_page *" p );
.BI "int  tui_viewdoc_text(const tui_viewdoc *" view ", char *" out ", size_t " size );
.BI "int  tui_viewdoc_check(const tui_viewdoc *" view ", const tui_table_col *" cols ,
.BI "                       int " ncols ", char *" msg ", size_t " size );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
One rule for every program: the key
.B ?
opens the help page of the view, and
.B d
on the page opens the description of the view in a dialog of its own.
A view registers once, in a
.BR tui_viewdoc :
its
.I name
(\(lqQueue\(rq: the description is titled \(lqQueue view\(rq), its
.I statement
(what the view is for; a view that is no table says what it shows and what each
part means), one
.B tui_viewdoc_col
(\fItitle\fR and a one-line \fItext\fR) for each column of its table in the
order of the table, and its
.I keys
(key and description in pairs,
.I nkeys
pairs).
Nothing is copied: the registration outlives the page.
.PP
.BR tui_viewdoc_open ()
makes the page: its first line is \(lqPress d: what this view is and what each
column means.\(rq, then the heading \(lqThis view\(rq with the keys of the view,
then \(lqEvery view\(rq with the
.I ncommon
pairs of
.IR common .
It returns \-1 with
.B EINVAL
or
.BR ENOMEM .
.PP
.BR tui_viewdoc_handle ()
gives it one event and returns the state:
.B TUI_DIALOG_OPEN
until it is closed,
.B TUI_DIALOG_OK
after.
.B d
(outside the search of the page, where it is text) opens the description:
the statement, a blank line, then one line \(lqTITLE  text\(rq for each column.
Esc, q or Backspace close the page, or the description and the page with it.
The other keys are those of
.BR tui_dialog_help (3):
scrolling and the search with
.BR / .
.BR tui_viewdoc_render ()
draws the page, or the description over it, centred in the canvas;
.BR tui_viewdoc_free ()
frees the page (safe twice, and after a failed open).
.PP
.BR tui_viewdoc_text ()
writes the text of the description as
.BR snprintf (3)
does and returns the length it needs.
.PP
.BR tui_viewdoc_check ()
is for the tests of the programs: it compares the titles of the columns of a
table with the registered ones, in order; a column without a title (a mark
column) is left out.
It returns 0 when they agree, \-1 when a column is not described or a
description names a column that is gone, and writes the first difference into
.IR msg .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
static const tui_viewdoc_col cols[] = {
    { "KEY", "the ticket" }, { "TITLE", "its title" } };
static const char *const keys[] = { "Enter", "open the row" };
static const char *const all[] = { "?", "this page", "Esc", "back" };
static const tui_viewdoc view = { "Queue", "The tickets in order.", cols, 2, keys, 1 };

/* in a test: */  assert(tui_viewdoc_check(&view, table_cols, n, msg, sizeof msg) == 0);
/* on ? */        tui_viewdoc_open(&page, &view, all, 2);
/* each event */  if (tui_viewdoc_handle(&page, &ev) != TUI_DIALOG_OPEN) tui_viewdoc_free(&page);
/* each frame */  tui_viewdoc_render(&page, canvas);
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tui_dialog_message (3),
.BR tui_table_init (3),
.BR libtuikit (7)
.PP
policies/tui-interface-model.md, \(lqThe help page and the view description\(rq.
